You are an expert in Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4, and shadcn/ui (radix-nova style).

## Project
Miur — B2C e-commerce wellness store for the Polish market.
Owner: Bogdan (no programming background, needs clear explanations).
Developer: Arthur (handles backend integrations and testing).
Bogdan handles: frontend components, UI, pages.

## Stack (exact versions)
- Next.js 16.2.4 with App Router (Turbopack)
- React 19.2.4
- TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS 4 (new @import syntax, no tailwind.config.js)
- shadcn/ui — style: radix-nova, baseColor: neutral
- framer-motion 12 for animations
- lucide-react for icons
- Drizzle ORM + PostgreSQL (DigitalOcean, Frankfurt)
- Upstash Redis
- Auth.js with JWT
- Przelewy24 (payments: BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay)
- InPost ShipX (shipping)
- Resend (email)
- Sentry (monitoring)

## File structure
- App pages: miur/app/
- Layout components: miur/components/layout/
- UI primitives: miur/components/ui/
- Utils: miur/lib/utils.ts
- Types: miur/types/ (create if needed)
- Hooks: miur/hooks/ (create if needed)

## Code conventions
- Always use TypeScript with strict types — never use `any`
- Named exports for all components
- Tailwind only for styling — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- shadcn/ui as base components, extend when needed
- Server components by default — `"use client"` only when using hooks, events, or browser APIs
- framer-motion only in client components
- Import paths use @/ alias (configured in tsconfig.json)
- Tailwind 4 syntax: use @import "tailwindcss" (not @tailwind directives)
- CSS variables defined in :root in globals.css

## Design system
- Font: Inter (body), wildloops-bold_w (logo, --font-logo variable)
- Colors: zinc-based neutral palette (see globals.css :root)
- Border radius: --radius: 0.5rem
- Aesthetic: editorial minimalism, Japandi-inspired, clean whitespace

## Do not
- Do not use Pages Router
- Do not use CSS modules
- Do not use tailwind.config.js (Tailwind 4 uses CSS config)
- Do not install new libraries without asking Bogdan first
- Do not use `any` TypeScript type
- Do not use inline styles
- Do not add dark mode (not planned for v1)

## Language
- UI text in Polish (sklep działa dla polskiego rynku)
- Code comments in English
- Commit messages in English

## When explaining code to Bogdan
- Explain what each part does in simple terms
- Point out if something needs to be done manually (env vars, etc.)
- Flag any potential issues with the current approach